window.KOS_EXAMS.reports = {"aqa-7516-1":{"title":"AQA 7516 (AS) Paper 1","habits":[{"sitting":null,"text":"**An identifier is just the name**: `LoadPuzzleFile`, not `def LoadPuzzleFile` or `LoadPuzzleFile()`; no data type with a variable. Extra code lost the mark every year."},{"sitting":null,"text":"**Paste the whole edited subroutine** as text, so the examiner can see where new code went. A capital letter should be at least 2 mm high when the EAD is printed."},{"sitting":null,"text":"Screen captures not made by your own code score nothing."},{"sitting":null,"text":"A \"describe\" mark needs the reason: \"reduces testing time\" scored nothing, but \"…because there is less code to test\" did."},{"sitting":null,"text":"A definition mark needs a standalone definition, not \"the opposite of the last one\"."},{"sitting":null,"text":"Don't say the same point twice in different words for a two-mark question."}],"notes":[{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q01","to":null,"marks":5,"leaf":"4.4.1.2","title":"trace table","points":["The usual dropped mark was the last one: **state the result** the algorithm produces."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q02","to":null,"marks":6,"leaf":"4.4.2.1","title":"labelling an FSM","points":["48% full marks. Trap: assuming one label per cell when the question said some need more than one."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q03.1","to":null,"marks":8,"leaf":"4.1.1.8","title":"random integers","points":["Traps: the wrong syntax, or the wrong range (0–6 for 1–6 inclusive). Later marks were still earned with a fixed value in place — keep going."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q06.2","to":null,"marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"a structure's roles","points":["It had several roles; most named one. Count the marks."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q08","to":null,"marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"decomposition","points":["\"Breaking a problem into sub-problems\" alone got one of two. It applies to the **problem**, not the solution; the spec's own definition helps."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q09.1","to":null,"marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"definite vs indefinite iteration","points":["Define each on its own: definite runs a number of times known before it starts; indefinite runs until a condition is met."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q10.1","to":null,"marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"exception handling","points":["\"Stops a crash\" is one mark; the other is that it handles **run-time** errors. \"Errors\" alone wasn't enough."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q11.1","to":null,"marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"subroutine","points":["\"A named section of code\" alone was incomplete: it is a named block that performs a specific task and can be **called** from elsewhere."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q12","to":null,"marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"protected coordinates (first modification)","points":["New checks go **after** the existing integer-conversion validation."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q13","to":null,"marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"Sudoku-style validation (six marks)","points":["Row and column were easy (two loops); the **sub-grid** check (MOD with nested loops, or a nine-way selection) was the discriminator."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q14","to":null,"marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"undo","points":["Students split into those who stopped after the call and those who finished. Traps: an empty string instead of a space; assuming the number of undos is one digit (−10 read as −1 then 0)."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q01","to":null,"marks":6,"leaf":"4.4.2.1","title":"state transition diagram","points":["Again: some states needed more than one label."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q02","to":null,"marks":5,"leaf":"4.4.1.2","title":"trace table","points":["Under 40% full marks; the usual error was the right value in the **wrong column**."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q03","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":null,"title":"4.1.1.13–14 global vs local","points":["Under half got both. \"Local has less scope\" is too vague: local exists only inside its subroutine while it runs; global is visible to the whole program for its whole run."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q04","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.4.1.2","title":"what an algorithm is","points":["Most scored nothing: \"a set of instructions\" isn't enough. A sequence of steps that can be followed to complete a task, and that always terminates."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q05.1","to":null,"marks":9,"leaf":"4.1.1.2","title":"pseudocode → code","points":["About 90% got 8–9. The dropped mark: the selection's logic **reversed**."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q11","to":null,"marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"three questions on one subroutine","points":["Marks were lost by putting a right answer under the **wrong part**. Read each part's ask."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q12.1","to":null,"marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"first modification","points":["The forgotten step was updating the status register."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q13.1","to":null,"marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"validating a line number","points":["Trap: a **hard-coded** upper bound. The program's length varies; use its length."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q14","to":"Q15","marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"later modifications","points":["Q14 was the most skipped, yet three quarters of attempts scored 3–4 of 4, with approaches the scheme hadn't foreseen still credited.","Q15: marks came for the menu change and input handling even when insert or delete was unfinished. Attempt it; then attempt its matching screenshot."]}]},"aqa-7516-2":{"title":"AQA 7516 (AS) Paper 2","habits":[{"sitting":"2023-06","text":"The real numbers are the rationals and irrationals together (a third missed it). Ordinal: a number giving an object's **position in an ordered sequence**, not just \"position\"."}],"notes":[{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q01.2","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.5.1.1","title":"irrational numbers","points":["Trap: \"an infinite decimal\". 0.333… is 1/3. Irrational = **can't be written as a fraction** of two integers."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q01.3","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.5.1.1","title":"shade one lozenge per column","points":["Under a quarter got both — mostly by shading more than one per column against the instructions."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q03.1","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.5.4.1","title":"range of 16-bit unsigned","points":["Trap: 65 536 and 1. It is **0 to 65 535**."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q03.2","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.5.4.1","title":"binary multiplication","points":["Write the trailing 0s on each partial product (10101__ is not 1010100); it went unpenalised this time but may not again."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q04.1","to":null,"marks":1,"leaf":"4.5.5.1","title":"character code","points":["\"A code for a character\" just restates the question: it is the **unique binary number** that represents a character in a character set."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q04.2","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.5.5.1","title":"why Unicode came in","points":["Answer **why it was introduced** (ASCII's 7/8 bits couldn't hold the world's scripts and symbols), not Unicode's advantages."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q04.3","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.5.5.3","title":"how parity works","points":["\"Checks the number of 1s\" was vague: the sender **counts the 1s** and sets the bit to make the total even/odd; the receiver counts again."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q04.5","to":null,"marks":3,"leaf":"4.5.6.10","title":"Vernam by hand","points":["Half full marks. Many did only the ASCII step; trap: **adding** the key instead of **XOR**. The ASCII step alone earns a mark — attempt it."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q05.2","to":null,"marks":3,"leaf":"4.5.6.1","title":"how an ADC works","points":["Under a quarter full marks. The wave becomes an **electrical signal**; the ADC samples that signal's amplitude at intervals and quantises each sample to an integer, then codes it in binary."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q06.2","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.6.1.3","title":"two other kinds of system software","points":["Trap: naming translators when the question said \"other\"; or OS functions. Utilities, libraries, operating system…"]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q06.3","to":"Q06.4","marks":3,"leaf":"4.6.3.1","title":"intermediate language","points":["Badly answered (1 in 8 left it blank). IL needs **further translation** on the target, by a virtual machine or a JIT compiler; it is used because it is processor-independent (portable)."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q07.4","to":"Q07.5","marks":7,"leaf":"4.6.5.1","title":"Boolean","points":["Spot when a truth table equals A·B instead of grinding laws.","Trap when expanding brackets: one half was AND, the other OR — the operators don't all become +. Practise many shapes."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q08.2","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.7.1.1","title":"RAM's role in running programs","points":["\"Stores data\" wasn't enough: it holds the **instructions and data of the running program** for the processor to fetch. Answer in context."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q08.4","to":"Q08.5","marks":3,"leaf":"4.7.1.1","title":"buses","points":["Data bus width: **more bits moved at once**. To double addressable memory, widen the **address bus** by one line. Many didn't attempt — naming a bus was a free guess."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q09.2","to":null,"marks":4,"leaf":"4.7.3.5","title":"a short assembly program","points":["Few full marks: the result was not **stored back** to memory. Traps: memory addresses in CMP instead of registers; a branch with no label."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q10.1","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.9.1.2","title":"start/stop bits","points":["Same as A-level 2022: start bit **synchronises the receiver's clock with the transmitter's**; stop bit lets the next start bit be seen."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q10.4","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.9.2.1","title":"star behaving as a bus","points":["Three quarters scored nothing. A switch can create a temporary path between two nodes using a bus protocol, so the physical star behaves logically as a bus."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q11","to":null,"marks":12,"leaf":"4.8.1","title":"+ 4.5.6.9 smart speakers and lossy compression","points":["Strong on ethics; better answers considered accents, languages and cultures.","Misconceptions: lossy compression anonymises the voice, or strips background noise and silence. It removes what the ear **can't perceive**, so the difference is hard to hear."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q03.2","to":null,"marks":1,"leaf":"4.5.4.1","title":"binary addition","points":["Fill in the **carry row** — the question asked for it, and the right sum without it lost the mark."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q03.3","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.5.4.3","title":"subtraction by two's complement","points":["Negate the number being **subtracted** (36 → −36) and add it to 27. Traps: negating 27, or negating both."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q03.4","to":null,"marks":1,"leaf":"4.5.4.3","title":"8-bit two's complement range","points":["−128 to 127. Trap: −256 to 255."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q03.5","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.5.4.4","title":"fixed point","points":["Traps: ignoring the point (221), or putting two bits after it instead of before (55.25). Read where the point sits."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q04.1","to":"Q04.2","marks":3,"leaf":"4.5.5.3","title":"majority voting vs parity","points":["\"More bits, more accurate\" scored nothing: each bit is sent three times and the receiver takes the majority, so a single flipped copy is corrected. Parity: faster, as fewer bits are sent."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q05.1","to":null,"marks":1,"leaf":"4.5.6.4","title":"bitmap size","points":["Trap: multiplying by the number of colours instead of the **colour depth** in bits."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q05.3","to":null,"marks":1,"leaf":"4.5.6.7","title":"sampling resolution","points":["Half failed: it is the **number of bits per sample**, not \"quality\"."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q05.5","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.5.6.8","title":"MIDI","points":["A third full marks; \"better quality\" scored nothing. Smaller files; easy to change notes or instruments."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q06.1","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.6.1.2","title":"libraries","points":["Not \"storing data\": prewritten, tested routines you can call — saves time, fewer errors."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q06.2","to":null,"marks":6,"leaf":"4.6.2.1","title":"high- vs low-level","points":["\"User-friendly\" and \"close to the hardware\" were Level 1. Name the features: selection and iteration structures, data structures, procedures, portability vs direct register/memory control."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q07.2","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.6.4.1","title":"write the Boolean expression","points":["Use AQA's notation (· + ⊕ and overbar); words were accepted this year only."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q07.3","to":null,"marks":4,"leaf":"4.6.5.1","title":"simplification","points":["The precedence trap again: in A·B + B·Ā, B + B is not the next step."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q08.1","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.7.3.1","title":"the status register","points":["Over half scored nothing. It holds flags (carry, zero, negative, overflow) set by the last operation and read by conditional branches."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q09","to":null,"marks":4,"leaf":"4.7.3.5","title":"assembly loop","points":["Capped at 3 when it didn't work every time: the loop label must sit **before the CMP** (the WHILE test), not before the body's ADD."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q10","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.7.3.7","title":"performance, in context","points":["Two thirds scored nothing with generic factors; tie the factor to the device in the question."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q11","to":null,"marks":9,"leaf":"4.8.1","title":"+ 4.5.6.4 an AI photo app","points":["Strong on ethics (bias, cultural assumptions); weaker on the camera, which capped answers at Level 2. Each sensor gives an electrical signal that is converted to binary."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q12.1","to":"Q12.3","marks":6,"leaf":"4.9.2.3","title":"+ 4.9.3.2 wireless","points":["SSID names the **network**, not the access point.","WPA2 **encrypts the data** — not just \"a password to join\".","MAC filtering in a coffee shop: impractical, staff must add every customer's device, and MACs can be spoofed — apply it to the scene."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q13.1","to":"Q13.2","marks":4,"leaf":null,"title":"4.9.2.1–2 star topology and client-server","points":["The centre of a star is a **switch**, not a server.","Client-server: the client **requests**, the server **responds**."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q14","to":null,"marks":3,"leaf":"4.7.4.1","title":"RFID in context","points":["Generic points (\"portable\") lacked depth; relate each feature to the scenario."]}]},"aqa-7517-1":{"title":"AQA 7517 Paper 1","habits":[{"sitting":"2022-06","text":"Use the Preliminary Material from September; test the Skeleton Program on the exam machines beforehand."},{"sitting":"2022-06","text":"**A screen capture not produced by your own running code scores nothing.** Spend that time making the code work."},{"sitting":"2022-06","text":"Paste code as text into the EAD; screenshots of code get cropped or are unreadable, and cropped lines lose marks."},{"sitting":"2022-06","text":"Crop test evidence carefully: an over-cropped capture lost the testing mark on working code (Q12.2)."},{"sitting":"2022-06","text":"Attempt the long modification questions: the first marks are for simple parts (declaring and initialising a variable in the right place). Over 15% skipped Q13 and gave those marks away."}],"notes":[{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q02.1","to":null,"marks":4,"leaf":"4.2.2.1","title":"removing from a circular queue","points":["Poor. Traps: removing from the rear; shuffling items \"up one\" (that is a linear queue); forgetting to **check for empty first**.","Marks: check empty; take the item at front; move front on by one, wrapping with MOD; reduce the size count."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q02.2","to":null,"marks":3,"leaf":"4.2.1.4","title":"static vs dynamic structures","points":["Few gave three. Beyond fixed size: memory allocated at compile time vs run time, possible wasted space vs overhead of pointers, heap use."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q02.5","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.2.3.1","title":"reversing a queue with a stack","points":["Common omission: putting the items **back into the queue** after popping them from the stack."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q03.1","to":"Q03.3","marks":4,"leaf":"4.4.1.1","title":"logic puzzle","points":["\"It's a contradiction\" alone scored nothing — say which statements conflict and why.","Trap: discarding a statement because it says the same as another."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q04.3","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.2.4.1","title":"short algorithm trace","points":["Only about 20% correct. Traps: returning several values; extra values for the counter. Follow the code exactly, line by line."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q04.5","to":null,"marks":6,"leaf":"4.3.1.1","title":"+ 4.1.1.16 recursive traversal trace","points":["About 10% full marks, though the early rows earned partial credit. Keep the call stack written down as you go."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q04.6","to":"Q04.8","marks":3,"leaf":"4.3.1.1","title":"what the algorithm is","points":["Recognising depth-first was easier than the purpose questions; some got these without a correct trace."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q05","to":null,"marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"reverse the order of the vowels in a string","points":["About a third fully working; finding the vowels alone got about half.","Traps: loop stopping before the **last character**; wrong combination of vowel conditions; failing with 0 or 1 vowels; indexing past the end.","Working shapes: collect vowels in a list, reverse it, put them back; or two pointers from each end; a stack or recursion also worked."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q06.3","to":null,"marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"protected","points":["Often described private instead. Protected: visible in the class **and its subclasses**. Not about who may edit the code."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q06.4","to":null,"marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"overriding","points":["Vague answers lost the mark. Tie it to **inheritance**: a subclass redefines a method it inherited, with the same signature."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q07.2","to":null,"marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"why not a set","points":["\"Values must be unique\" is true but irrelevant. A set has **no order**, and a deck needs one."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q07.3","to":"Q07.4","marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"a hash table for the cards","points":["Most gave \"the hash gives the storage location\". Fewer gave collision handling, or hashing the card number because it is unique. Suitability: direct access in constant time."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q08.2","to":"Q08.3","marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"identifiers and stack frames","points":["An identifier must clearly be about the thing asked (the hand).","A stack-frame answer must name what **this** subroutine's frame holds, not the generic list."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q10","to":null,"marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"a regular expression","points":["Most couldn't write it accurately; many didn't use `|` for alternation."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q11","to":null,"marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"input validation","points":["Over half full marks. Traps: combining two conditions wrongly; no error message. Recursive retries often ignored the returned value, which broke the game afterwards."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q12","to":null,"marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"count tool cards in the deck","points":["About 40% full marks. Traps: counting one tool type twice; wrong compound conditions; a loop missing the last card."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q13","to":null,"marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"a one-use blasting cap","points":["About 15% full marks. Traps: initialising the \"used\" flag where it **resets every turn**; an off-by-one in the position check (the user's position needs −1 for the index).","The test must show everything asked, including the second attempt."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q14","to":null,"marks":null,"leaf":null,"title":"a trap card subclass","points":["Very few full marks. Traps: inheriting from Card instead of DifficultyCard; code that can pick an unmet challenge or change several; missing a change in GetCardFromDeck.","Working shapes: a list of the met challenges' indexes, or check that one exists and draw at random until a met one comes up."]}]},"aqa-7517-2":{"title":"AQA 7517 Paper 2","habits":[],"notes":[{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q01.1","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.5.2.1","title":"number bases — binary → hex","points":["Asked: *describe* how to convert binary to hex.","Most: did the conversion instead of describing it (no marks), or said \"split into 4-bit groups\" then described each group's value vaguely.","Marks: split into nibbles from the right (1); each nibble → one hex digit, with how (1)."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q01.2","to":null,"marks":1,"leaf":"4.5.2.1","title":"why hex, not binary","points":["Trap: \"hex uses fewer digits to store\". It is always STORED in binary; hex is only shorter to read and write for humans."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q02.1","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.9.1.1","title":"parallel transmission","points":["Most got \"several wires\"; the second mark needs **one bit per wire, at the same time** — \"data/packets sent together\" was too vague."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q02.4","to":"Q02.5","marks":2,"leaf":"4.9.1.2","title":"start and stop bits","points":["Poorly understood. \"Shows where the transmission starts/ends\" scored nothing.","Start bit: wakes the receiver and **synchronises the receiver's clock with the sender's** — name both clocks.","Stop bit: lets the next start bit be recognised / gives the receiver time to process the byte."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q03.3","to":null,"marks":4,"leaf":"4.6.5.1","title":"Boolean simplification","points":["Only about a quarter got full marks.","Trap 1: simplifying A + Ā to 1 when the A was ANDed with (B + 1) — **AND binds tighter than OR**; respect precedence first.","Trap 2: applying De Morgan across mixed operators in one step. It only extends to several operators at once when they are **all the same**."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q04.3","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.6.1.4","title":"functions of an operating system","points":["Naming a function (\"memory management\"), even in a sentence, scored nothing. Describe it: *regions of memory are allocated to processes*.","\"Provides a user interface\" needs developing: the OS is a layer that hides the hardware's complexity."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q05.1","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.5.4.4","title":"fixed point → decimal","points":["Traps: treating the −32 place as +32; or writing −20 and .6875 separately as −20.6875. It is −20 **+** 0.6875 = −19.3125."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q05.2","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.5.4.8","title":"why normalise","points":["Vague answers (\"more accurate\", \"easier to read\") scored nothing.","Marks: **maximum precision** for the bits available; **one unique representation** per number (so equality tests are simple)."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q05.3","to":"Q05.4","marks":5,"leaf":"4.5.4.4","title":"floating point","points":["Traps: moving the point the wrong way; exponent sign (+9 for −7).","Negative values: write the positive in fixed point first, THEN take two's complement. Writing \"−23\" then \"+.25\" gives −22.75.","**Show working** — it earns credit when the final answer slips."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q05.5","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.5.4.5","title":"relative error","points":["Traps: a negative absolute error; dividing by the stored value instead of the true one; arithmetic slips."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q06","to":null,"marks":12,"leaf":"4.7.4.1","title":"+ 4.8.1 bar codes, RFID and a loyalty scheme","points":["Covering only two of the three areas capped the level.","Legal/ethical: consent, GDPR duties, who sees the data and for what. Don't assume data was taken without consent.","Misconception: a bar's colour is a bit. Bars differ in **width**."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q07.2","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.10.1","title":"ER degrees","points":["Trap: drawing one-to-one because an animal is in one place *now* — the data kept history, so it was one-to-many. Read what the table stores."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q07.3","to":null,"marks":3,"leaf":"4.10.4","title":"CREATE TABLE","points":["Under a quarter full marks. Traps: data type before the field name; missing commas between field definitions. Syntax must be exact."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q07.4","to":null,"marks":7,"leaf":"4.10.4","title":"SELECT with a date range","points":["Structure and the join condition were usually right; the date conditions that catch **every** overlapping stay were the hard part."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q07.5","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.10.3","title":"adding a redundant attribute","points":["Advantage: one-table query, no join. Disadvantage: redundancy → extra storage → possible **inconsistency** and harder updates."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q08.1","to":null,"marks":3,"leaf":"4.9.2.2","title":"peer-to-peer vs client-server","points":["Misconceptions: all traffic passes through the server; if the server fails the network fails. Neither is true."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q08.2","to":null,"marks":3,"leaf":"4.9.2.2","title":"which suits a student house","points":["Use the context (few devices, users trust each other, choose what to share). \"Cheaper\" needs the why (no server to buy)."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q08.3","to":null,"marks":3,"leaf":"4.9.3.1","title":"DNS","points":["\"Addresses\" without \"IP\" scored nothing. Better: FQDN → IP; a hierarchy of servers holding a distributed database; unknown names are forwarded."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q09.2","to":null,"marks":5,"leaf":"4.7.3.5","title":"assembly trace","points":["Under a quarter full marks. Traps: LSR shifted left; a fractional value after a right shift; forgetting the final STR to memory."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q09.4","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.6.2.1","title":"why write in assembly","points":["Faster or smaller code. Not \"doesn't need translating\" (it does) and not hardware access when the task doesn't need it."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q10.1","to":null,"marks":3,"leaf":"4.5.6.7","title":"sound duration","points":["Trap: MB → bytes as ×1,000 instead of ×1,000,000."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q11","to":null,"marks":3,"leaf":"4.9.4.11","title":"thin vs thick client","points":["Only about a third scored. \"Powerful server\", \"cheap computer\" are not A-level answers — say RAM, cores, storage, and **which machine**."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q12.3","to":"Q12.4","marks":5,"leaf":"4.12","title":"functional programming","points":["Write a list result **in brackets**. Tracing the recursive functions was the discriminator; the purpose must be specific (average °C from a list of °F, not \"averages a list\")."]},{"sitting":"2022-06","q":"Q13.2","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.7.4.2","title":"why secondary storage","points":["\"Non-volatile\" alone or \"more storage\" alone scored nothing — explain.","Misconception: main memory is volatile (ROM isn't); secondary storage is a backup of RAM (it isn't)."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q01.1","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.5.6.7","title":"sound file size in MiB","points":["Usually 1 of 2. Traps: ÷1000 instead of **÷1024** for mebi; forgetting **÷8** to go from bits to bytes."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q01.3","to":null,"marks":1,"leaf":"4.5.6.1","title":"what turns binary into a waveform","points":["About half wrote ADC. Playing sound back is a **DAC**."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q02.1","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.9.4.1","title":"packet fields","points":["Most named one field; only about a quarter named two (e.g. source and destination IP, sequence number, TTL, checksum, payload)."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q02.2","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.5.5.3","title":"checksum","points":["Vague: \"checks the data is correct\" / \"an algorithm on the data\".","Marks: detects data **changed in transit**; computed from the payload by a calculation the receiver repeats. (It can't prove the data was right when sent.)"]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q02.3","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.9.3.1","title":"a router's role","points":["\"Sends it to its destination\" was too thin. Routing is **hop by hop**: each router picks the next hop for the packet."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q03.1","to":"Q03.3","marks":3,"leaf":"4.5.6.10","title":"Caesar and substitution ciphers","points":["Caesar: the slip was the last letter wrapping round past Z.","Shared weakness: a letter always maps to the same letter, so **frequency analysis** works. \"Few keys / brute force\" isn't shared (the substitution cipher has many keys).","Avoid \"random\" unless you mean it; \"more random\" scored nothing."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q03.4","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.5.6.10","title":"Vernam perfect security","points":["Say \"**the key** is used once / truly random / as long as the message\", not \"it\"."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q04.1","to":null,"marks":12,"leaf":"4.7.3.2","title":"+ 4.7.3.7 fetch–execute and performance","points":["Weakest stage was **execute**; fetch got most detail. Cover all three stages with the registers.","Be precise on improvements: more cores means instructions run **simultaneously**, not just \"more per second\"."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q04.2","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.7.3.6","title":"interrupts","points":["Define it: a signal from a device or program asking for the processor's urgent attention. It does not stop the fetch–execute cycle (it is checked at the end of each cycle), and it is not about instruction priority."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q05.1","to":null,"marks":5,"leaf":"4.10.3","title":"completing a normalised design","points":["Traps: a redundant ScreenNumber in Booking (it follows from ShowingID); one relation for a booking of several seats (needs two)."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q05.2","to":"Q05.3","marks":4,"leaf":"4.10.4","title":"DELETE and integrity","points":["The errors: an unneeded table in the query; the date **unquoted**.","Deleting showings with bookings breaks **referential integrity** / foreign keys — use the terms."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q05.4","to":"Q05.5","marks":2,"leaf":"4.9.4.10","title":"REST and CRUD","points":["Weak area. The URL causes a query on the server. GET→SELECT, POST→INSERT, PUT→UPDATE, DELETE→DELETE."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q06.1","to":"Q06.2","marks":5,"leaf":"4.5.4.4","title":"floating point","points":["Same traps as 2022: point moved the wrong way (6.5 for 13/128); −23 then +.25 giving −22.75. Convert the positive, then negate."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q06.3","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.5.4.5","title":"naming errors","points":["Most couldn't name them. Overflow ≠ stack overflow."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q06.4","to":null,"marks":1,"leaf":"4.5.4.7","title":"more precision, same bits","points":["Take bits from the exponent for the mantissa, or imply the bit next to the point (it is always the opposite of the sign bit) to gain one."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q07.3","to":null,"marks":10,"leaf":"4.7.3.5","title":"assembly: byte → two ASCII hex codes","points":["The hardest assembly task on this spec so far. Traps: - operands written in binary; - a missing `#` for immediate values; - AND with 240 but no LSR #4 afterwards; - code after a branch target runs on into the next label, adding a second constant (55 then 48) by accident.","Practise with AQA's own instruction set before the exam."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q08.1","to":null,"marks":1,"leaf":"4.11.1","title":"velocity","points":["It means data arriving and needing processing **very** fast — beyond what a traditional relational system could keep up with."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q08.3","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.12","title":"why functional code distributes well","points":["Weak. Give the features with their effect: **immutable** data and **no side effects**, so pieces can run on different servers in any order. A single word (\"immutable\") was not enough."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q09.3","to":null,"marks":4,"leaf":"4.6.5.1","title":"Boolean simplification","points":["The two traps again: B̄ + B → 1 too early (AND before OR); cancelling NOTs that cover different parts of the expression instead of applying De Morgan."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q10.2","to":null,"marks":1,"leaf":"4.9.1.2","title":"synchronous transmission","points":["Poor. The clocks are **kept** synchronised, or a clock signal travels with the data."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q10.3","to":null,"marks":1,"leaf":"4.5.5.3","title":"limits of parity","points":["An **even number of flipped bits** goes undetected; errors are found, never corrected. \"Multi-bit errors\" is wrong (odd counts are caught)."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q11.1","to":null,"marks":3,"leaf":"4.9.4.1","title":"the transport layer","points":["Most gave \"splits into packets\" only. Add port numbers, end-to-end connection, sequencing. Common error: describing the network layer."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q11.2","to":null,"marks":1,"leaf":"4.9.3.1","title":"gateway vs router","points":["Few knew: a gateway **translates between protocols** when networks differ."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q11.4","to":null,"marks":2,"leaf":"4.9.4.2","title":"well-known ports","points":["The second mark: the sender starts the connection, so the server's port has to be fixed and known."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q11.5","to":null,"marks":6,"leaf":"4.9.3.2","title":"asymmetric encryption and digital signatures","points":["Traps: forgetting that **each** party has its own key pair; using the wrong key at a step; \"compare the digest with the message\" — compare the decrypted digest with a **recomputed** digest of the message."]},{"sitting":"2023-06","q":"Q12.1","to":null,"marks":3,"leaf":"4.12.3.1","title":"tracing a recursive function","points":["Base case and arguments were fine; combining the returned values on the way back up was where marks went."]}]}};
